      "code_hash": "928c38427c9d827695eebc4959ecbb2e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"chiral-z-decays\">Chiral Z decays</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><a href=\"/\">Browse all notebooks</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/weak_decays.py\">W and top decays</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"/?file=hep/diphoton.py\">Two-photon annihilation</a></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generate <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z\\to f\\bar f||)</marimo-tex> from the Standard Model and retain the fermion mass,\nleft- and right-chiral couplings, and the Z's longitudinal polarization.\nChoose a neutrino, charged lepton, up-type quark or down-type quark to reproduce\nthe four classes in the\n<a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/EW/Tree/Z-FFbar\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc example</a>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The three initial Z polarizations are averaged; final spins and colors are\nsummed. Fermion and antifermion are distinct, so no identical-particle factor\nis needed.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "d9bec9d9a353ea52437a41636529893b",
      "outputs": [
